The paper was removed by arXiv administrators because it was judged to contain substantial copied or overlapping material from earlier arXiv papers—specifically **gr-qc/0410004**, **gr-qc/0603075**, and material overlapping **gr-qc/0608111**.

In arXiv terms, this usually means a violation of their policies on:

- **plagiarism**: copying text, equations, figures, structure, or results from other papers without proper attribution or permission;
- **excessive overlap/self-plagiarism or duplicate submission**: reusing large portions of another work, even if related, without making a sufficiently original contribution;
- **misrepresentation of authorship/originality**.

So the reason was not necessarily that the physics was wrong, but that the submission was considered insufficiently original and copied/overlapped too much with existing works.
